---
import Layout from '../layouts/StandardLayout.astro';
import { currentSite } from '../lib/site';
---
{currentSite(import.meta.env.PUBLIC_SITE_KEY) === 'agdr' ? <Layout title="Specification"><section class="page"><p class="eyebrow">AgDR 1.2.0 · Published</p><h1>Agent Decision Record Specification.</h1><p class="lede">The normative specification defines the file location, required frontmatter, status values, decision body and validation rules for consequential technical decisions made by agents.</p><div class="callout"><strong>Normative source.</strong><br /><a href="https://github.com/me2resh/agent-decision-record/blob/main/SPEC.md">Read SPEC.md in the source repository</a>. The repository is the version-controlled source for this published reference.</div><h2>What AgDR records</h2><p>An AgDR records what an agent decided, the context that led to the decision, and the rationale that should remain available after the session ends.</p><h2>Interoperability</h2><p>Typed relationships may be added as an extension. They are informative until adopted by the AgDR specification.</p></section></Layout> : <Layout title="Specification"><section class="page"><p class="eyebrow">ORBIT v0.1 · Draft</p><h1>Keep execution aligned with durable outcomes.</h1><p class="lede">An ORBIT Plan is a portable declaration of durable software intent and outcomes designed to be reconciled against current reality before execution work is materialised.</p><div class="callout"><strong>A Plan is not a backlog.</strong><br />ORBIT keeps intent durable while deriving only the next bounded execution slice from current reality.</div><h2>Normative sections</h2><p>Version 0.1 defines Plans, outcomes, acceptance criteria, Project Snapshots, reconciliation, observations, discoveries, execution slices, provenance, staleness and extensions.</p><h2>Execution neutrality</h2><p>ORBIT does not define coding agents, issue trackers, branch workflows, CI/CD, model providers, source-control hosting, or orchestration systems.</p></section></Layout>}
